Credit

  Adapted from the Microduck by Pollen Robotics,
  https://github.com/pollen-robotics/microduck_rl

  Their repository states: "3D model files are licensed under Creative
  Commons BY-SA-NC". It names no version of the licence; version 4.0 is used
  here. The shells were taken from a pack of 15 meshes exported from their
  simulation model, which carries no licence or author of its own; its part
  list matches their model.

What was changed

  - every shell scaled by 1.25;
  - the model re-split into printable parts, each one closed solid, and
    simplified to a tolerance of 0.45 mm;
  - the original's servo mounts replaced by cradles and horn plates for
    TinkerKit Braccio servos (SR431, SR311) and 9 g servos, the hip pitch
    axis moved 4.75 mm forward, the hip roll axis 4.5 mm down and 5 mm
    inward and the ankle axis 6.5 mm down so that those servos and the
    parts on them clear each other;
  - the thigh covers, feet and lower head shell cut back where the new parts
    turn;
  - the soles widened towards the centre line (a web);
  - a frame added in the trunk with a back plate for two controller boards;
  - a seat for a camera board added behind the eye.

What this means for you

  You may copy, print and adapt these parts for non-commercial purposes if
  you give the credit above, say what you changed and share your version
  under the same licence. You may not sell the parts or prints of them.
  Pollen Robotics sell the original robot.

  "Microduck" is the name of Pollen Robotics' robot and is used here only to
  say what these parts were adapted from. This project is not affiliated with
  or endorsed by Pollen Robotics.

What is not covered

  build.py, the script that generates the parts, is MIT licensed
  (SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT). The source meshes are not in this
  directory.

Comb feet

  left_foot_comb.stl and right_foot_comb.stl are the two feet above with
  part of the web cut away and fingers added that cross the centre line
  between the fingers of the other foot. They are made from left_foot.stl
  and right_foot.stl by microduck/look/combfeet.py (MIT); their dimensions
  are in comb_feet.json. They are adapted from the same model, the Microduck
  by Pollen Robotics, and carry the same licence and credit as the other
  files in this directory.
